{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:69e9c1663668ad68","name":"Fighter Groups","source":{"id":"source:reference-69e9c1663668ad68","title":"Fighter Groups","revision":18703,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:35:16Z","sha256":"4cfec8347f092cb21b420961a0344507958e3fa6322a515a7f5879b27aae5c6b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18703","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Fighter%20Groups&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-69e9c1663668ad68","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Fighter Groups are formations of two to six ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," that act as a single unit, greatly speeding up large battles. Anyone ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," skill can join a Fighter Group by moving into the same space as a willing allied ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," of the same size. The Fighter Group then acts on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative Count"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative_Count"}," of the last ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to join, occupying the same space on the battle grid. The Fighter Group's leader (designated by mutual consent) makes all the decisions and actions for the group.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Joining a Fighter Group ends your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Actions","referenceId":"reference:ff8059dc6752afdd"}," for the round; any unused Actions (including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Readied Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Readied_Actions"},") are lost. If you choose to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Delay"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Delay"}," on the Fighter Group's turn, you automatically leave the group. Once the leader of a Fighter Group is chosen, it can be changed only once per round on the Fighter Group's turn. When the first ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," joins another to form the Fighter Group, the first leader is chosen at that time.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Fighter Groups can use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Maneuvers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Maneuvers","referenceId":"reference:d34674a1187e91cd"}," only if every member of the Fighter Group has that maneuver. When the maneuver is used, every member of the Fighter Group uses it. If a member of the group has an [",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Attack Pattern"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_Pattern"}]},"] maneuver active when it joins the group, its effects are lost (the Fighter Group is, itself, like an [",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Attack Pattern"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_Pattern"}]},"]).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Fighter Group uses the group leader's attack bonus and skill modifiers, but the worst ",{"tag":"a","children":["Defenses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Defenses","referenceId":"reference:0d85b79fde210d9c"}," and damage for each weapon type in the group. When attacked, the group leader may either designate a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," operated by a generic crew as the target or determine the target randomly. On the group's turn, the group leader can gain one of the following benefits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["Act as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Battery"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Battery"}," (+2 on attacks per additional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},", plus the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Narrow Salvo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Narrow_Salvo"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Proximity Spread"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Proximity_Spread"}," abilities)."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":["Gain a +2 circumstance bonus per additional ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," on either opposed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," checks made for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dogfighting"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dogfighting"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," checks made to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Sensors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Sensors","referenceId":"reference:1bf2e88f5409e504"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," checks."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
